fail[3]: [3, 2, 1].
fail[5]: [3, 0, -1].
hint: Swap when the left item is **smaller** than the right one.
hint: Each pass then carries the smallest unsorted item to the end.
hint: Keep the swapped flag, and break after a pass with no swaps.
right: Flipping the comparison flips the order; the early stop makes a list that's already in descending order take one pass.
wrong: Use the same passes, but swap when `items[i] < items[i + 1]`, so smaller items sink to the end. Stop after a pass with no swaps.

