wrong[['Ana', 'Cy', 'Ben'] ['Ben', 'Cy', 'Ana']]: Sorting by age puts Ben, 25, first.
hint: Both calls put Ben, the youngest, first.
hint: The difference is what happens when Ana and Cy, both 30, are compared.
right: `['Ben', 'Ana', 'Cy'] ['Ben', 'Cy', 'Ana']`: the stable version keeps Ana before Cy; swapping ties reverses them.
wrong: Pass 1 swaps Ana and Ben (30 > 25) in both versions. Then Ana meets Cy: the first version leaves them, the second swaps them. So the names come back as Ben, Ana, Cy and Ben, Cy, Ana.

